-- CA.seg: what each declaration's informal text opens.
-- Notation (opened to expose the shape of a type, "A x", a pair, Id Bool _ true):
--   Cl Iff Cap Sub Eqv tau M scA PsiP Down Tr LT OK RS NZ Mc Lex
-- Computational definitions are opened only where the text says "by definition":
--   cin, psiC in their clause lemmas; C in ca-mk, ca-ok, ca-in and ca-sup (substitution);
--   tilde in r-tilde (a~ is the first value of card); omF, isOT in r-omF (Omega_I = I);
--   lt, cmp2, isOT, ... in the closed computations om1-lt-I, om1-OK, ca-zero, ca-I.
-- cin-psi also opens lt/cmp2/fwd: unfolding cin at psi evaluates its Boolean lt a k
-- (a checker artefact, not a step of the text).
